WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.368 --> 00:00:03.482
(whooshing)

00:00:03.482 --> 00:00:05.001
- Initiate the action.

00:00:05.001 --> 00:00:05.834
- Take action.

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:06.720
- Taking action.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:07.770
- Taking action.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:08.603
- Do the action.

00:00:08.603 --> 00:00:09.954
- Act Now!

00:00:09.954 --> 00:00:11.187
- Took action.

00:00:11.187 --> 00:00:13.403
- Hello Believe Vision, my
name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:13.403 --> 00:00:16.208
My one word is believe and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:16.208 --> 00:00:18.976
will solve all of the
world's major problems.

00:00:18.976 --> 00:00:20.785
So to help you in your journey today,

00:00:20.785 --> 00:00:23.605
we're going to learn how to take action.

00:00:23.605 --> 00:00:24.899
And also guys, if you're watching,

00:00:24.899 --> 00:00:26.745
if you hear something that
really resonates with you

00:00:26.745 --> 00:00:28.451
please leave it down
in the comments below,

00:00:28.451 --> 00:00:30.646
put quotes around it,
you might win a prize.

00:00:30.646 --> 00:00:31.835
But also when you write it down,

00:00:31.835 --> 00:00:35.199
it's much more likely to
stick with yourself as well.

00:00:35.199 --> 00:00:36.508
Enjoy.

00:00:36.508 --> 00:00:39.091
(upbeat music)

00:00:47.629 --> 00:00:49.802
- You speak to businesses and companies

00:00:49.802 --> 00:00:52.465
and leadership teams
and employees and stuff.

00:00:52.465 --> 00:00:53.548
Without mentioning names,

00:00:53.548 --> 00:00:55.106
I don't want to put you on the spot but

00:00:55.106 --> 00:00:59.171
have you gone and talked to a
company that's been in trouble

00:00:59.171 --> 00:01:02.723
and then spoken to their team
and then checked in on them

00:01:02.723 --> 00:01:05.685
after you've spoken to
their leadership team

00:01:05.685 --> 00:01:07.149
and what did that look like,

00:01:07.149 --> 00:01:09.201
did you notice a noticeable change?

00:01:09.201 --> 00:01:11.741
Did they come to you and
tell you that this has helped

00:01:11.741 --> 00:01:13.527
our organization out and our culture

00:01:13.527 --> 00:01:16.728
is much improved because of it?

00:01:16.728 --> 00:01:18.200
- You mean does my (bleep) work?

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.200
(audience laughing)

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:30.122
I mean.

00:01:30.122 --> 00:01:32.089
(audience laughing)

00:01:32.089 --> 00:01:32.922
Sure.

00:01:35.113 --> 00:01:39.426
Here's the problem with my
stuff, you got to do it.

00:01:39.426 --> 00:01:41.676
And I am not anybody's like

00:01:43.105 --> 00:01:44.904
you know, mom or dad.

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:46.458
I'm not going to do it for you.

00:01:46.458 --> 00:01:48.412
And I have a very laissez-faire approach.

00:01:48.412 --> 00:01:50.445
I once had a client,

00:01:50.445 --> 00:01:52.734
this is a bunch of years ago

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:54.964
that said, what guarantee do I have

00:01:54.964 --> 00:01:57.594
that you're stuff will work?

00:01:57.594 --> 00:01:58.842
To which my answer was,

00:01:58.842 --> 00:01:59.675
none.

00:02:00.562 --> 00:02:03.552
Like, I'm giving you a tool.

00:02:03.552 --> 00:02:04.814
You can, it's like a hammer,

00:02:04.814 --> 00:02:06.366
you can use it broadly or narrowly.

00:02:06.366 --> 00:02:07.711
You can build a table,
you can build a house.

00:02:07.711 --> 00:02:08.623
It's the same tool.

00:02:08.623 --> 00:02:09.487
You can use it for marketing.

00:02:09.487 --> 00:02:12.558
You can use it to completely
revitalize your entire culture.

00:02:12.558 --> 00:02:13.391
And even though I'm going to sale you

00:02:13.391 --> 00:02:15.200
the most beautiful hammer,

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.308
I'm not going to guarantee

00:02:16.308 --> 00:02:18.401
the structural integrity of the house.

00:02:18.401 --> 00:02:19.234
Right?

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:20.341
It's your business.

00:02:20.341 --> 00:02:21.369
You want to ignore all my stuff.

00:02:21.369 --> 00:02:22.687
Ignore it, I don't care.

00:02:22.687 --> 00:02:24.967
And if your business collapses,
you know what happens to me?

00:02:24.967 --> 00:02:25.800
Nothing.

00:02:27.187 --> 00:02:29.088
Like, I don't mean to be cold about it.

00:02:29.088 --> 00:02:31.159
Like of course, I want the
people I work with to do well

00:02:31.159 --> 00:02:32.981
but it's not mine.

00:02:32.981 --> 00:02:36.122
It's theirs and I take no
emotional responsibility

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:37.428
for the decisions they make.

00:02:37.428 --> 00:02:40.818
So yes, there are many people
that I have had the pleasure

00:02:40.818 --> 00:02:41.651
of working with.

00:02:41.651 --> 00:02:43.038
Some who worked for
dysfunctional organizations

00:02:43.038 --> 00:02:45.585
that went on the hard journey

00:02:45.585 --> 00:02:47.779
of completely changing the way they lead

00:02:47.779 --> 00:02:49.757
and completely revitalizing their culture

00:02:49.757 --> 00:02:51.860
and it has great success.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:54.557
It's not because of me,
it's because of them, right.

00:02:54.557 --> 00:02:56.392
At the same time, there
are many people who came in

00:02:56.392 --> 00:02:59.347
and they're like, what an
amazing speech and did nothing.

00:02:59.347 --> 00:03:01.929
You know, thanks that was great, you know.

00:03:01.929 --> 00:03:05.786
And I don't, of course, it's
going to fail, you know.

00:03:05.786 --> 00:03:09.030
So, I think that we have too much,

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:10.786
especially in the consulting world,

00:03:10.786 --> 00:03:12.501
or the design world,

00:03:12.501 --> 00:03:15.210
everybody's so paternalistic about it.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:17.305
And designers are famous for this right.

00:03:17.305 --> 00:03:20.248
They get so personally
offended when the client

00:03:20.248 --> 00:03:22.248
chooses the wrong thing.

00:03:23.119 --> 00:03:24.314
Uh, such idiots!

00:03:24.314 --> 00:03:26.272
Don't they know we're trying to help them?

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:28.870
(audience laughing)

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:29.953
Or who cares?

00:03:30.849 --> 00:03:32.952
Like it's their freaking business, right.

00:03:32.952 --> 00:03:34.858
That's what you find, I've had that.

00:03:34.858 --> 00:03:36.400
Instead of arguing with somebody

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.918
for them to make the right choice,

00:03:37.918 --> 00:03:40.078
'cause we genuinely want to help them.

00:03:40.078 --> 00:03:40.940
What I have found is,

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.498
if you push the accountability on them,

00:03:42.498 --> 00:03:45.068
'cause when we argue, we're
taking accountability.

00:03:45.068 --> 00:03:48.443
This is better, this will help you.

00:03:48.443 --> 00:03:51.001
We're taking responsibility,
accountability.

00:03:51.001 --> 00:03:52.859
But if we say look,

00:03:52.859 --> 00:03:54.157
we've been doing this a bunch of years.

00:03:54.157 --> 00:03:56.993
We know more about design than you do.

00:03:56.993 --> 00:03:59.962
I'm telling you, for every
reason that I can outline for you

00:03:59.962 --> 00:04:02.215
why this will help you more.

00:04:02.215 --> 00:04:04.331
But if you don't want
to do it, that's fine.

00:04:04.331 --> 00:04:06.421
It's your business, do what you want.

00:04:06.421 --> 00:04:07.963
The minute you switch the accountability

00:04:07.963 --> 00:04:09.004
and put it all on them.

00:04:09.004 --> 00:04:11.481
Amazingly, they're much
more open to your opinion.

00:04:11.481 --> 00:04:12.949
(audience laughing)

00:04:12.949 --> 00:04:14.622
Because now they're responsible.

00:04:14.622 --> 00:04:16.911
- One night, Chris has gone to bed.

00:04:16.911 --> 00:04:18.746
I'd been struggling,
struggling, struggling.

00:04:18.746 --> 00:04:21.771
We still had all the same problems.

00:04:21.771 --> 00:04:22.604
We struggled on the house,

00:04:22.604 --> 00:04:25.134
still facing bankruptcy,
still fighting like crazy.

00:04:25.134 --> 00:04:27.051
I was still unemployed.

00:04:28.224 --> 00:04:31.125
They still hadn't figured
out like the solution yet

00:04:31.125 --> 00:04:33.255
for the business.

00:04:33.255 --> 00:04:34.707
And I was about to turn off the TV

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:36.977
and there on the TV

00:04:36.977 --> 00:04:38.293
there was this rocket launching

00:04:38.293 --> 00:04:40.498
and I thought oh my gosh.

00:04:40.498 --> 00:04:41.415
That is it!

00:04:43.998 --> 00:04:46.882
I am going to launch myself out of bed

00:04:46.882 --> 00:04:49.616
like a rocket ship, like NASA!

00:04:49.616 --> 00:04:51.995
Right here and launch me out of that bed.

00:04:51.995 --> 00:04:53.542
And I'm going to move so fast

00:04:53.542 --> 00:04:55.687
that I don't think.
- Hm.

00:04:55.687 --> 00:04:57.459
- I'm going to beat my brain.

00:04:57.459 --> 00:05:00.709
Now, here's a really interesting point.

00:05:01.952 --> 00:05:06.076
I talk a lot about your
instincts and inner wisdom.

00:05:06.076 --> 00:05:08.504
And we can get get into
this a little bit later

00:05:08.504 --> 00:05:09.918
but a lot of us talk about the fact

00:05:09.918 --> 00:05:11.137
that you have a gut feeling.

00:05:11.137 --> 00:05:14.063
But what all this research
that I've done for the book

00:05:14.063 --> 00:05:15.759
and all the speaking that I do,

00:05:15.759 --> 00:05:17.246
what I've discovered that's fascinating

00:05:17.246 --> 00:05:20.586
is actually when you set goals,
when you have an intention

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:22.972
on something that you want
to change about your life,

00:05:22.972 --> 00:05:24.449
your brain helps you.

00:05:24.449 --> 00:05:27.107
What it does it is opens up a checklist

00:05:27.107 --> 00:05:29.033
and then your brain goes to work

00:05:29.033 --> 00:05:31.300
trying to remind you.
- Yeah.

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:33.460
- Of that intention that you set.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:36.686
And it's really important
to develop the skill

00:05:36.686 --> 00:05:38.286
and I say that word purposefully.

00:05:38.286 --> 00:05:42.174
The skill of knowing how
to hear that inner wisdom

00:05:42.174 --> 00:05:44.382
and that intention kicking in.

00:05:44.382 --> 00:05:46.479
And leaning into it quickly.

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:48.746
So for me, my brain saying that's it.

00:05:48.746 --> 00:05:49.854
Right there.

00:05:49.854 --> 00:05:52.315
Move as fast as a rocket, Mel.

00:05:52.315 --> 00:05:54.476
I wanted to change to my life.

00:05:54.476 --> 00:05:56.900
And I think most people that are miserable

00:05:56.900 --> 00:06:00.714
or that are really like dying to be great

00:06:00.714 --> 00:06:02.142
and dying to have more,

00:06:02.142 --> 00:06:03.326
we want to change.

00:06:03.326 --> 00:06:05.301
We want to live a better life.

00:06:05.301 --> 00:06:07.373
We want to create more for our families.

00:06:07.373 --> 00:06:09.337
We want to be happier.

00:06:09.337 --> 00:06:11.004
The desire is there.

00:06:11.908 --> 00:06:14.218
Again it's about how do you
go from knowledge to action

00:06:14.218 --> 00:06:16.523
so the first thing in this
story that's important

00:06:16.523 --> 00:06:19.295
is realizing that the answer was in me.

00:06:19.295 --> 00:06:22.573
And my mind was telling me, pay attention.

00:06:22.573 --> 00:06:23.621
Could have also been the bourbon.

00:06:23.621 --> 00:06:25.059
(laughing)

00:06:25.059 --> 00:06:26.895
I had a couple of Manhattan's that night.

00:06:26.895 --> 00:06:30.895
Anyway, the next morning,
the alarm goes off and

00:06:31.913 --> 00:06:33.912
I pretended NASA was there.

00:06:33.912 --> 00:06:34.936
It's the stupidest story.

00:06:34.936 --> 00:06:37.496
I literally went five,
four, three, two, one.

00:06:37.496 --> 00:06:40.495
I counted out loud and then I stood up.

00:06:40.495 --> 00:06:42.737
And I'll never forget standing there

00:06:42.737 --> 00:06:43.570
in my bedroom.

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:45.653
It was dark, it was cold.

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:48.590
It was winter in Boston.

00:06:49.481 --> 00:06:51.759
And for the first time in three months,

00:06:51.759 --> 00:06:56.367
I had beaten my habit of
hitting the snooze button.

00:06:56.367 --> 00:06:57.200
I couldn't believe it.

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:59.429
And I thought, wait a minute.

00:06:59.429 --> 00:07:00.436
Counting backwards,

00:07:00.436 --> 00:07:02.070
that is the dumbest thing I've ever heard

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:03.581
in my entire life.

00:07:03.581 --> 00:07:05.508
Well the next morning, I
used it again it worked.

00:07:05.508 --> 00:07:07.516
The next morning I used
it again and it worked.

00:07:07.516 --> 00:07:09.805
The next morning I used
it again and it worked.

00:07:09.805 --> 00:07:13.247
And then I started to notice
something really interesting.

00:07:13.247 --> 00:07:15.994
There were moments all day long.

00:07:15.994 --> 00:07:17.077
All day long.

00:07:18.135 --> 00:07:22.144
Just like that five second moment in bed.

00:07:22.144 --> 00:07:24.061
Where I knew knowledge,

00:07:24.986 --> 00:07:27.218
what I should do.

00:07:27.218 --> 00:07:30.543
And if I didn't move within five seconds,

00:07:30.543 --> 00:07:33.617
my brain would step in
and talk me out of it.

00:07:33.617 --> 00:07:35.689
Every human being has
a five second window.

00:07:35.689 --> 00:07:38.761
Might even be shorter for you.

00:07:38.761 --> 00:07:40.529
You have about a five second window

00:07:40.529 --> 00:07:44.284
in which you can move from idea to action

00:07:44.284 --> 00:07:47.245
before your brain kicks into full gear

00:07:47.245 --> 00:07:50.927
and sabotages any change in behavior.

00:07:50.927 --> 00:07:53.355
'Cause remember your
brain is wired to stop you

00:07:53.355 --> 00:07:54.595
from doing things that are comfortable

00:07:54.595 --> 00:07:57.215
or uncertain or scary.

00:07:57.215 --> 00:08:01.018
It's your job to learn how
to move from those ideas

00:08:01.018 --> 00:08:03.052
that could change everything

00:08:03.052 --> 00:08:05.094
into acting on them.

00:08:05.094 --> 00:08:08.231
- People want to know
how to stop the laziness

00:08:08.231 --> 00:08:12.398
and they want to know how to
stop the procrastination and

00:08:13.316 --> 00:08:16.130
they have some idea in
their head, you know,

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:17.880
some kind of a vision

00:08:20.338 --> 00:08:22.338
of what they want to do.

00:08:23.566 --> 00:08:24.775
But they don't know where to start.

00:08:24.775 --> 00:08:26.630
They don't know where
to start it, you know.

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:29.172
They don't know where to start.

00:08:29.172 --> 00:08:31.301
And to this day, hey,

00:08:31.301 --> 00:08:34.594
where do I start and when's
the best time to start.

00:08:34.594 --> 00:08:38.711
And I have a very simple answer for that.

00:08:38.711 --> 00:08:39.544
Here.

00:08:40.444 --> 00:08:41.277
And now.

00:08:43.954 --> 00:08:45.102
That's it.

00:08:45.102 --> 00:08:47.331
You want to improve?

00:08:47.331 --> 00:08:48.976
You want to get better?

00:08:48.976 --> 00:08:52.904
You want to get on a workout
program or a clean diet?

00:08:52.904 --> 00:08:55.321
You want to start a business?

00:08:56.618 --> 00:08:58.853
You want to write a book or make a movie

00:08:58.853 --> 00:09:00.755
or build a house or a computer

00:09:00.755 --> 00:09:04.088
or put together some mobile application?

00:09:06.858 --> 00:09:08.441
Where do you start?

00:09:10.751 --> 00:09:12.506
You start right here.

00:09:12.506 --> 00:09:16.856
And when do you start,
you start right now.

00:09:16.856 --> 00:09:19.794
You initiate the action aggressively.

00:09:19.794 --> 00:09:20.627
You go.

00:09:22.809 --> 00:09:26.488
'Cause the idea isn't
going to execute itself.

00:09:26.488 --> 00:09:28.514
And the book isn't going to write itself.

00:09:28.514 --> 00:09:30.377
And the weights out in the gym,

00:09:30.377 --> 00:09:32.412
they're not going to move themselves.

00:09:32.412 --> 00:09:36.079
You have to do it and
you have to do it now.

00:09:38.557 --> 00:09:41.861
And that means, you got
to stop thinking about it

00:09:41.861 --> 00:09:43.714
and stop dreaming about it.

00:09:43.714 --> 00:09:46.580
And stop researching every aspect of it.

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:47.907
And reading all about it.

00:09:47.907 --> 00:09:50.394
And debating the pros and cons of it.

00:09:50.394 --> 00:09:52.061
Just start doing it.

00:09:55.479 --> 00:09:57.229
Take that first step.

00:09:58.757 --> 00:10:00.340
And make it happen.

00:10:01.731 --> 00:10:03.208
Get after it.

00:10:03.208 --> 00:10:05.708
And get after it here and now.

00:10:07.969 --> 00:10:09.409
- Take action.

00:10:09.409 --> 00:10:10.996
Whatever you want to do you.

00:10:10.996 --> 00:10:12.327
Whatever you're thinking about.

00:10:12.327 --> 00:10:15.970
You will not get it until
you get take action.

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:17.091
Make that move.

00:10:17.091 --> 00:10:18.188
Make it a small step.

00:10:18.188 --> 00:10:21.529
If you want a house, go get
a rug, you know what I mean?

00:10:21.529 --> 00:10:24.381
If you want a new car, go
get some car freshener.

00:10:24.381 --> 00:10:25.418
Take action.

00:10:25.418 --> 00:10:29.126
Make this thing happen for
you and it will happen.

00:10:29.126 --> 00:10:31.043
Action, action, action.

00:10:31.975 --> 00:10:34.436
You know one thing that

00:10:34.436 --> 00:10:38.351
I can really attribute to every failure

00:10:38.351 --> 00:10:39.268
in my life.

00:10:40.619 --> 00:10:43.452
Whether it be personal, financial,

00:10:45.164 --> 00:10:48.842
in any kind of way, business, whatever.

00:10:48.842 --> 00:10:51.112
It's because of a lack

00:10:51.112 --> 00:10:53.541
of my attempt to take action.

00:10:53.541 --> 00:10:55.892
I did not take action.

00:10:55.892 --> 00:10:59.892
And it kind of changed,
once I got the fact that

00:11:00.963 --> 00:11:02.380
action is the key

00:11:03.512 --> 00:11:06.034
it changed my life in many, many ways.

00:11:06.034 --> 00:11:07.511
- I think stress,

00:11:07.511 --> 00:11:09.786
you can be, I think one of the things

00:11:09.786 --> 00:11:12.396
that's very important
to note about stress,

00:11:12.396 --> 00:11:17.321
is that stress primarily
comes from not taking action

00:11:17.321 --> 00:11:21.100
over something that you
can have some control over.

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:24.771
So, if I find that some particular thing

00:11:24.771 --> 00:11:26.698
is causing me to have stress,

00:11:26.698 --> 00:11:29.115
that's a warning flag for me.

00:11:30.047 --> 00:11:31.352
What it means is,

00:11:31.352 --> 00:11:34.534
there's something that I
haven't completely identified

00:11:34.534 --> 00:11:36.717
perhaps in my conscious mind

00:11:36.717 --> 00:11:39.553
that is bothering me and I haven't

00:11:39.553 --> 00:11:41.137
yet taken any action on it.

00:11:41.137 --> 00:11:43.635
I find as soon as I identify it

00:11:43.635 --> 00:11:44.914
and make the first phone call

00:11:44.914 --> 00:11:46.574
or send off the first email message

00:11:46.574 --> 00:11:48.706
or whatever it is that we're going to do

00:11:48.706 --> 00:11:52.521
to start to address that
situation, even if it's not solved,

00:11:52.521 --> 00:11:54.582
the mere fact that we're addressing it,

00:11:54.582 --> 00:11:57.264
dramatically reduces any
stress that might come from it.

00:11:57.264 --> 00:12:00.541
So stress comes from ignoring things

00:12:00.541 --> 00:12:04.244
that you shouldn't be ignoring,
I think in a large part.

00:12:04.244 --> 00:12:06.071
So, stress doesn't come.

00:12:06.071 --> 00:12:10.377
People get stress wrong all
the time, in my opinion.

00:12:10.377 --> 00:12:13.790
Stress doesn't come from
hard work, for example.

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:15.802
You know, you can be
working incredibly hard

00:12:15.802 --> 00:12:16.852
and loving it.

00:12:16.852 --> 00:12:19.251
And likewise, you can be out of work

00:12:19.251 --> 00:12:21.909
and incredibly stressed over that.

00:12:21.909 --> 00:12:25.458
So, and likewise if you kind
of use that as an analogy

00:12:25.458 --> 00:12:27.188
for what I was just talking about.

00:12:27.188 --> 00:12:28.481
If you're out of work,

00:12:28.481 --> 00:12:30.418
but you're going though, you know

00:12:30.418 --> 00:12:33.113
a disciplined approach of you know,

00:12:33.113 --> 00:12:34.966
a series of job interviews and so on

00:12:34.966 --> 00:12:37.137
and working to remedy that situation,

00:12:37.137 --> 00:12:38.819
you're going to be a lot less stressed

00:12:38.819 --> 00:12:40.620
than if you're just worrying about it

00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:41.940
and doing nothing.

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:45.426
- One of the functions of
belief is taking action.

00:12:45.426 --> 00:12:46.802
We did a survey of about two thousand

00:12:46.802 --> 00:12:49.536
top entrepreneurs and we
noticed that one of the things

00:12:49.536 --> 00:12:53.183
that people who win in that
world have is a bias for action.

00:12:53.183 --> 00:12:55.461
If they have an
inspiration, they act on it.

00:12:55.461 --> 00:12:57.424
I mean how many of you
have ever had a great idea,

00:12:57.424 --> 00:12:58.679
talked about it, thought about it,

00:12:58.679 --> 00:12:59.692
didn't do it.

00:12:59.692 --> 00:13:01.726
And then someone else
did it and was successful

00:13:01.726 --> 00:13:03.590
and you went, darn I
should have done that.

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:05.574
Maybe it was buy that piece of property.

00:13:05.574 --> 00:13:07.994
We all have that piece of
property we wished we bought.

00:13:07.994 --> 00:13:09.308
You know.
(audience murmuring)

00:13:09.308 --> 00:13:11.515
Anyway, so we're going to be looking at

00:13:11.515 --> 00:13:14.338
the idea that taking action
is part of law of attraction.

00:13:14.338 --> 00:13:16.277
See a lot of people think
you can just sit in your room

00:13:16.277 --> 00:13:18.791
meditate, visualize
having the perfect car,

00:13:18.791 --> 00:13:20.912
the perfect house, the
perfect relationship.

00:13:20.912 --> 00:13:22.960
Then it'll kind of just come to you.

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:25.238
And I always say unless you
live at the bottom of a hill,

00:13:25.238 --> 00:13:27.140
(audience laughing)

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:28.676
where there's a road,

00:13:28.676 --> 00:13:29.845
there's probably not
going to be a Cadillac

00:13:29.845 --> 00:13:31.122
show up in your living room, right.

00:13:31.122 --> 00:13:32.202
(audience laughing)

00:13:32.202 --> 00:13:35.165
So, think about this, the last six letters

00:13:35.165 --> 00:13:37.102
of the word attraction spell what?

00:13:37.102 --> 00:13:37.993
(audience murmuring)

00:13:37.993 --> 00:13:39.783
A-C-T-I-O-N, action.

00:13:39.783 --> 00:13:42.340
Now there's two kinds of
action that are critical.

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:43.771
There's obvious action.

00:13:43.771 --> 00:13:45.186
If you want a certain kind of car,

00:13:45.186 --> 00:13:46.877
you should go down and test drive it.

00:13:46.877 --> 00:13:48.671
You should find out how much it costs.

00:13:48.671 --> 00:13:51.157
You should see what it
costs to maintain it.

00:13:51.157 --> 00:13:52.816
You should go, you know, spend,

00:13:52.816 --> 00:13:55.082
I like to test drive a
car, three or four times.

00:13:55.082 --> 00:13:56.815
Go down to the dealer, take a camera.

00:13:56.815 --> 00:13:58.581
Stick my head out the
window, say a picture of me.

00:13:58.581 --> 00:13:59.833
I'll be back to buy it, you know.

00:13:59.833 --> 00:14:00.931
(audience laughing)

00:14:00.931 --> 00:14:02.236
Put it up on my refrigerator.

00:14:02.236 --> 00:14:03.969
Look at it very day.

00:14:03.969 --> 00:14:05.895
Eventually, you know,
those kinds of things

00:14:05.895 --> 00:14:07.474
produce a car, right.

00:14:07.474 --> 00:14:08.719
Saving for it, so forth.

00:14:08.719 --> 00:14:11.854
But there are also things
called inspired actions.

00:14:11.854 --> 00:14:14.261
All of a sudden, you get an
inspiration to do something

00:14:14.261 --> 00:14:16.469
and you didn't know what it was.

00:14:16.469 --> 00:14:17.614
You don't have the sense of like,

00:14:17.614 --> 00:14:19.238
how is this rationally going to make sense

00:14:19.238 --> 00:14:21.311
for me to move forward in my life.

00:14:21.311 --> 00:14:22.359
I'll give you an example.

00:14:22.359 --> 00:14:24.406
A friend of mine, Dr. Ignatius Piazza,

00:14:24.406 --> 00:14:26.431
graduates chiropractic school.

00:14:26.431 --> 00:14:28.785
He wants to move Monterey
near Pebble Beach

00:14:28.785 --> 00:14:30.164
where the golf course is.

00:14:30.164 --> 00:14:31.128
And he gets there and he says

00:14:31.128 --> 00:14:33.200
to the local Chiropractic Association,

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:34.188
I'd like to join you.

00:14:34.188 --> 00:14:35.677
I'd like you to help me
get my practice started.

00:14:35.677 --> 00:14:37.408
And they said, we don't
need any more chiropractics.

00:14:37.408 --> 00:14:40.650
We have one chiropractic for
ever eight people in this area.

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:41.916
It's too many.

00:14:41.916 --> 00:14:43.162
Now he could have say, okay,

00:14:43.162 --> 00:14:45.854
let the external reality
control his internal experience

00:14:45.854 --> 00:14:46.999
but he didn't do that.

00:14:46.999 --> 00:14:49.755
He said, I'm going to think about this

00:14:49.755 --> 00:14:51.329
and visualize it and believe in it.

00:14:51.329 --> 00:14:53.144
And something will come that I will do.

00:14:53.144 --> 00:14:54.694
And what came to him to do,

00:14:54.694 --> 00:14:57.717
was to take six months
before he opened his office

00:14:57.717 --> 00:14:59.483
and put a pin where he wanted his office

00:14:59.483 --> 00:15:01.235
and then concentric circles,

00:15:01.235 --> 00:15:03.279
knock on every door in every neighborhood

00:15:03.279 --> 00:15:04.874
saying hi, I'm a new doctor in town.

00:15:04.874 --> 00:15:06.226
Can I ask you a few questions?

00:15:06.226 --> 00:15:07.939
You know I'm starting this practice.

00:15:07.939 --> 00:15:10.818
Should I open from five
til nine in the morning

00:15:10.818 --> 00:15:12.543
or should I be open from
five until nine at night

00:15:12.543 --> 00:15:14.420
for people who have nine to five jobs.

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:15.650
Which would be better?

00:15:15.650 --> 00:15:17.808
Should I advertise in
this paper or that paper?

00:15:17.808 --> 00:15:19.770
Should I call it Ignatius
Piazza Chiropractic

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:21.710
or Chiropractic West?

00:15:21.710 --> 00:15:23.353
Then his last question was
if I have an open house,

00:15:23.353 --> 00:15:25.606
would you like to receive an invitation?

00:15:25.606 --> 00:15:27.365
If they said yes, he wrote it down.

00:15:27.365 --> 00:15:31.070
Now over six months, he
knocked on 12,500 doors.

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:35.411
Talked to 6,500 people and
gathered over 4000 names

00:15:35.411 --> 00:15:37.250
of people who said yes,
I'd like an invitation

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:38.640
to your open house.

00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:40.897
Now when he opened his
office six months later

00:15:40.897 --> 00:15:42.804
in a town that did not
need another chiropractor

00:15:42.804 --> 00:15:44.653
according to the professionals,

00:15:44.653 --> 00:15:48.011
his first month in
practice he netted $72,000.

00:15:48.011 --> 00:15:49.693
(audience murmuring)

00:15:49.693 --> 00:15:51.069
In his first year in practice,

00:15:51.069 --> 00:15:54.482
his gross income was
over a million dollars.

00:15:54.482 --> 00:15:56.070
I was giving a talk and
mentioned this story

00:15:56.070 --> 00:15:57.337
just about five years ago

00:15:57.337 --> 00:16:00.065
and this happened about 25 years ago.

00:16:00.065 --> 00:16:01.942
Someone said, he knocked on my door.

00:16:01.942 --> 00:16:05.377
(audience laughing)

00:16:05.377 --> 00:16:07.111
And he left his card.

00:16:07.111 --> 00:16:08.661
And two years later, I
needed a chiropractor

00:16:08.661 --> 00:16:09.756
and I called him.

00:16:09.756 --> 00:16:11.148
Because we work with people we know,

00:16:11.148 --> 00:16:12.694
we've had an experience with right?

00:16:12.694 --> 00:16:14.024
So he trusted his intuition.

00:16:14.024 --> 00:16:15.386
He took action on it.

00:16:15.386 --> 00:16:18.828
Other people would say, oop,
guess I can't have what I want.

00:16:18.828 --> 00:16:21.046
You got to be willing to take the action.

00:16:21.046 --> 00:16:25.614
- You can't just wait
for inspiration, to act.

00:16:25.614 --> 00:16:27.994
That's the biggest mistake people make.

00:16:27.994 --> 00:16:30.211
Don't wait to be inspired
to do the action.

00:16:30.211 --> 00:16:32.812
You have to do the action first
and then you'll be inspired.

00:16:32.812 --> 00:16:34.118
So what I would do is I
would sit there and draw

00:16:34.118 --> 00:16:35.349
the comic and I would come up with it.

00:16:35.349 --> 00:16:37.373
But some days I come home
from school, sit down and go

00:16:37.373 --> 00:16:38.968
I'm just going to wait for
the inspiration to hit me.

00:16:38.968 --> 00:16:41.160
I'm going to wait for the
idea to come fully formed.

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:42.577
And when I got a joke,

00:16:42.577 --> 00:16:43.883
then I'll go draw it.

00:16:43.883 --> 00:16:45.673
And I would sit there for
maybe three or four hours

00:16:45.673 --> 00:16:47.074
(laughing) and then go, alright screw it,

00:16:47.074 --> 00:16:48.448
I got to get up, I got to do the process.

00:16:48.448 --> 00:16:50.190
I got to sit there and just start drawing.

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:53.763
I don't even know why or
how I'm going to get there

00:16:53.763 --> 00:16:55.066
and then two things would come together

00:16:55.066 --> 00:16:55.899
and then it would be oh, there's an idea

00:16:55.899 --> 00:16:56.732
oh there's the first para,

00:16:56.732 --> 00:16:57.565
the second para.

00:16:57.565 --> 00:16:58.398
And then it would come together.

00:16:58.398 --> 00:17:00.248
Always, it would not take very long.

00:17:00.248 --> 00:17:01.843
I would fight that process so much

00:17:01.843 --> 00:17:02.717
because what was I doing.

00:17:02.717 --> 00:17:05.216
I was waiting for
inspiration before I acted.

00:17:05.216 --> 00:17:06.902
It's always the other way around.

00:17:06.902 --> 00:17:09.604
Act first, then the inspiration will come.

00:17:09.604 --> 00:17:10.934
Draw first.

00:17:10.934 --> 00:17:13.023
Then the inspiration will come.

00:17:13.023 --> 00:17:15.769
Just start shooting, then
the inspiration will come.

00:17:15.769 --> 00:17:18.085
Just start moving, then
the inspiration will come.

00:17:18.085 --> 00:17:18.918
Don't wait.

00:17:18.918 --> 00:17:20.523
So many people wait

00:17:20.523 --> 00:17:21.700
or tell you they're
going to write this novel

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:23.466
or they're going to do this or
their going to make this film,

00:17:23.466 --> 00:17:24.401
they never do it.

00:17:24.401 --> 00:17:27.094
Because they're waiting for
all this stuff to come to them.

00:17:27.094 --> 00:17:28.819
It comes through doing it.

00:17:28.819 --> 00:17:30.414
- Don't wait.

00:17:30.414 --> 00:17:31.247
Go.

00:17:31.247 --> 00:17:32.080
Do it.

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:32.913
Act.

00:17:32.913 --> 00:17:34.446
Now.

00:17:34.446 --> 00:17:37.230
And really accepting, we need
you, we need you, we need you.

00:17:37.230 --> 00:17:38.480
You are the one percent,

00:17:38.480 --> 00:17:40.441
you're the percent that says

00:17:40.441 --> 00:17:41.334
I'm going to wake up.

00:17:41.334 --> 00:17:42.370
You're the light workers.

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:45.235
You are the ones that
have accepted this call

00:17:45.235 --> 00:17:46.759
in this lifetime, at this time.

00:17:46.759 --> 00:17:49.319
You have decided to wake
up and chosen to say

00:17:49.319 --> 00:17:50.954
yes, I'm here to be of greater service

00:17:50.954 --> 00:17:52.813
than just to feed myself, right.

00:17:52.813 --> 00:17:53.963
I'm here to feed the world.

00:17:53.963 --> 00:17:54.885
I'm here to give love.

00:17:54.885 --> 00:17:57.080
I'm here to be an
expression of that truth.

00:17:57.080 --> 00:17:58.830
Don't hold that back.

00:18:01.001 --> 00:18:02.418
Don't play small.

00:18:03.568 --> 00:18:06.234
We can't, we need you.

00:18:06.234 --> 00:18:08.420
And so really if you
or anyone in this room

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:12.402
who has been sitting on that book idea

00:18:12.402 --> 00:18:13.694
waiting a little bit longer

00:18:13.694 --> 00:18:16.448
before you start that t-shirt training,

00:18:16.448 --> 00:18:18.033
or doing ten more teacher trainings

00:18:18.033 --> 00:18:19.455
before you actually teach.

00:18:19.455 --> 00:18:22.651
(audience laughing)

00:18:22.651 --> 00:18:24.900
If that's you guys,

00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:27.570
start and the pressure will be off.

00:18:27.570 --> 00:18:30.638
I can't begin to tell you, I
could cry just saying this,

00:18:30.638 --> 00:18:32.917
the day I taught Ego Eradicator

00:18:32.917 --> 00:18:35.478
I was two weeks into my teaching training

00:18:35.478 --> 00:18:37.904
and I said F it, let's go!

00:18:37.904 --> 00:18:41.164
And I just went and I
felt so much pressure off.

00:18:41.164 --> 00:18:43.318
I felt so much lift.

00:18:43.318 --> 00:18:46.661
Because I just knew I felt
this technology must be shared.

00:18:46.661 --> 00:18:47.765
I can't hold it.

00:18:47.765 --> 00:18:49.099
I can't keep it from myself.

00:18:49.099 --> 00:18:50.703
I can't just sit in my
apartment by myself like this

00:18:50.703 --> 00:18:51.546
(sniffing)

00:18:51.546 --> 00:18:55.316
I got to give this.
(audience laughing)

00:18:55.316 --> 00:18:58.168
And sharing it, the
pressure, it just lifted.

00:18:58.168 --> 00:19:00.306
It was like, aw, thank you.

00:19:00.306 --> 00:19:01.565
Thank you, thank you.

00:19:01.565 --> 00:19:03.078
And I wasn't the perfect teacher.

00:19:03.078 --> 00:19:05.539
And I look back and I was
teaching Ego Eradicator wrong.

00:19:05.539 --> 00:19:06.970
Everyone's arms were like this.

00:19:06.970 --> 00:19:08.189
Everyone was breathing backwards.

00:19:08.189 --> 00:19:09.386
It was a mess but I did it.

00:19:09.386 --> 00:19:11.338
And I started.

00:19:11.338 --> 00:19:13.442
And in those moments
when we just get to go,

00:19:13.442 --> 00:19:14.275
just go.

00:19:15.178 --> 00:19:16.023
The pressure is off

00:19:16.023 --> 00:19:18.561
and then we clear the
path and we are guided

00:19:18.561 --> 00:19:20.005
to the next right action.

00:19:20.005 --> 00:19:23.418
And that is the most magnificent
thing you can do right now.

00:19:23.418 --> 00:19:24.666
- I find it quite inspiring.

00:19:24.666 --> 00:19:27.807
You were in film publicity, originally.

00:19:27.807 --> 00:19:29.482
And then at a certain point,

00:19:29.482 --> 00:19:31.347
you decided that you wanted to direct.

00:19:31.347 --> 00:19:35.920
Can you tell us how you
got from there to here?

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:38.319
- Well I was one of those
ladies standing on the side.

00:19:38.319 --> 00:19:40.078
You know, and they work hard.

00:19:40.078 --> 00:19:42.563
And no one ever really
gives them the shout out.

00:19:42.563 --> 00:19:44.716
I thank you all, the publicist
in the corner, you know.

00:19:44.716 --> 00:19:46.857
(audience clapping)

00:19:46.857 --> 00:19:49.416
And as a person who loved
film and wanted to make film,

00:19:49.416 --> 00:19:51.023
you're standing there
supporting film makers,

00:19:51.023 --> 00:19:53.726
telling their stories and it's
something that I love doing.

00:19:53.726 --> 00:19:56.021
But for me there was always a

00:19:56.021 --> 00:19:57.824
little bit of, I don't know, not jealousy,

00:19:57.824 --> 00:20:00.299
but just like wow, that's
great what they're doing.

00:20:00.299 --> 00:20:02.210
And so at the moment, when I actually

00:20:02.210 --> 00:20:04.384
started to write and tried
to direct my own stuff,

00:20:04.384 --> 00:20:06.688
I was still doing publicity
for other people's films.

00:20:06.688 --> 00:20:08.598
I was trying to make my own films.

00:20:08.598 --> 00:20:11.036
I was asking for
permission, pitching people,

00:20:11.036 --> 00:20:12.975
trying to get contacts and network

00:20:12.975 --> 00:20:15.341
and do all the things that don't matter.

00:20:15.341 --> 00:20:17.314
Because the only thing
that matters is your work.

00:20:17.314 --> 00:20:19.346
And so, when I finally realized that

00:20:19.346 --> 00:20:21.203
and started to make small things and try

00:20:21.203 --> 00:20:22.554
to move them around festivals

00:20:22.554 --> 00:20:26.071
and just you know, just share my work,

00:20:26.071 --> 00:20:28.416
the energy behind that positive intention

00:20:28.416 --> 00:20:29.960
started the ball rolling.

00:20:29.960 --> 00:20:33.162
And I've only been making
films for five years.

00:20:33.162 --> 00:20:37.876
And I only quit my job
full-time three years ago.

00:20:37.876 --> 00:20:39.083
Because I was still
holding on to publicity

00:20:39.083 --> 00:20:41.390
as a security blanket.

00:20:41.390 --> 00:20:43.178
And so yeah,

00:20:43.178 --> 00:20:44.761
you know, I look at

00:20:45.665 --> 00:20:46.839
each year that's passed

00:20:46.839 --> 00:20:48.366
and all I've tried to do is continue

00:20:48.366 --> 00:20:50.446
to make work whether I have the money

00:20:50.446 --> 00:20:52.722
to make a film, a narrative, a doc,

00:20:52.722 --> 00:20:55.526
a commercial, a TV show,

00:20:55.526 --> 00:20:56.359
directed an episode of Scandal,

00:20:56.359 --> 00:20:57.213
(audience clapping)

00:20:57.213 --> 00:20:59.299
a documentary about Venus Williams,

00:20:59.299 --> 00:21:02.041
whatever I, a story I want to
tell through whatever medium,

00:21:02.041 --> 00:21:04.227
short medium, TV medium,

00:21:04.227 --> 00:21:06.857
commercial medium,
full-length, documentary,

00:21:06.857 --> 00:21:11.277
feature, that's something that
I really learned from Spike.

00:21:11.277 --> 00:21:13.138
Lee, not Jones, I'm
sure Jones is nice but.

00:21:13.138 --> 00:21:14.343
(audience laughing)

00:21:14.343 --> 00:21:15.962
I was talking to a lady, she
was like Spike Jones is a.

00:21:15.962 --> 00:21:17.222
No lady, Spike Lee.

00:21:17.222 --> 00:21:19.547
(audience laughing)

00:21:19.547 --> 00:21:22.128
But you know, remember he
did commercials with Jordan.

00:21:22.128 --> 00:21:25.308
He's done almost as many
docs as he's done narratives.

00:21:25.308 --> 00:21:27.685
He's made a film every
year for the past 20 years.

00:21:27.685 --> 00:21:29.656
I mean, he's really the blue print of

00:21:29.656 --> 00:21:30.834
just not even a black film maker,

00:21:30.834 --> 00:21:33.750
a film maker who has just
continued to make work.

00:21:33.750 --> 00:21:35.315
And so that's how we're here now.

00:21:35.315 --> 00:21:39.482
- Your book is titled, Nothing
to Lose, Everything to Gain.

00:21:40.653 --> 00:21:42.952
What does that title mean to you?

00:21:42.952 --> 00:21:44.201
- You know it's a mindset.

00:21:44.201 --> 00:21:45.321
So, it's a mindset that I had

00:21:45.321 --> 00:21:46.457
when I was on the streets,

00:21:46.457 --> 00:21:48.289
and when I lived in boys homes

00:21:48.289 --> 00:21:49.945
and when I was in juvenile hall.

00:21:49.945 --> 00:21:52.095
And the essence is, when
you have nothing to lose,

00:21:52.095 --> 00:21:54.273
you either are backed into a corner or,

00:21:54.273 --> 00:21:56.213
and you cower and you submit

00:21:56.213 --> 00:21:57.484
or you fight your way out

00:21:57.484 --> 00:21:59.931
and so, I've been backed
into a corner a few times

00:21:59.931 --> 00:22:01.670
both when I was a kid but then also

00:22:01.670 --> 00:22:02.753
in my professional career

00:22:02.753 --> 00:22:04.875
when I decided to become an entreprenuer.

00:22:04.875 --> 00:22:06.269
When the recession hit, you know,

00:22:06.269 --> 00:22:07.689
I had to apply that same mindset.

00:22:07.689 --> 00:22:09.472
- Now as your mantra, why do you think

00:22:09.472 --> 00:22:12.679
so many people don't live
with that mindset today?

00:22:12.679 --> 00:22:14.510
I mean, there's a lot of fear out there.

00:22:14.510 --> 00:22:15.474
Fear of the unknown.

00:22:15.474 --> 00:22:17.821
- Yeah, you know what, fear is a trap.

00:22:17.821 --> 00:22:19.723
And people are domesticated so to speak.

00:22:19.723 --> 00:22:21.693
So, you know, they're comfortable.

00:22:21.693 --> 00:22:24.070
And if they just realize that
they have nothing to lose,

00:22:24.070 --> 00:22:26.253
you know, these middle
class folks that are,

00:22:26.253 --> 00:22:27.635
you know, they think they
have something to lose.

00:22:27.635 --> 00:22:30.105
They think that they're
reputation with their neighbors

00:22:30.105 --> 00:22:32.633
or their credit or their
Louis Vuitton luggage,

00:22:32.633 --> 00:22:33.831
or whatever it is

00:22:33.831 --> 00:22:35.344
is worth holding on to.

00:22:35.344 --> 00:22:36.542
If they just ventured out there,

00:22:36.542 --> 00:22:38.728
started a business, took action,

00:22:38.728 --> 00:22:40.709
they'd realize there's a better life.

00:22:40.709 --> 00:22:42.101
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:22:42.101 --> 00:22:43.045
I hope you enjoy.

00:22:43.045 --> 00:22:45.242
I love to know what did
you take from this video

00:22:45.242 --> 00:22:47.863
that you're going to
immediately apply somehow

00:22:47.863 --> 00:22:49.639
to your life or to your business.

00:22:49.639 --> 00:22:51.142
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:22:51.142 --> 00:22:53.288
I'm really excited to
see what you have to say.

00:22:53.288 --> 00:22:54.780
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:22:54.780 --> 00:22:55.957
I believe in you.

00:22:55.957 --> 00:22:57.981
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself.

00:22:57.981 --> 00:23:00.318
And whatever your one word is,

00:23:00.318 --> 00:23:01.537
much love.

00:23:01.537 --> 00:23:02.573
I'll see you soon.

00:23:02.573 --> 00:23:04.906
